I'd put all of the routing in one file and turn the payments override into a field on each service, so it's no longer code.

The override is what makes the three drift apart, because it repeats facts the CSVs already hold. `FINANCE_SERVICES` is a hand-copied list of billing's services. `URGENT` repeats the sev1 and sev2 rows that already map to `page`. Its channel result is always `page`, which those severities already get, so the only thing it really changes is the team. If someone adds a billing service or moves sev2 to Slack, the override silently stops matching.

I'd replace both CSVs with a single `routing.toml`:

```toml
[channels]
sev1 = "page"
sev2 = "page"
sev3 = "slack"
sev4 = "email"

[services]
checkout      = { team = "storefront" }
search        = { team = "discovery" }
catalog       = { team = "discovery" }
# billing's rotation is not staffed overnight, so pages go to finance on-call
payments      = { team = "billing", page_team = "finance-oncall" }
ledger        = { team = "billing", page_team = "finance-oncall" }
notifications = { team = "platform" }
auth          = { team = "identity" }
inventory     = { team = "fulfilment" }
shipping      = { team = "fulfilment" }
```

`route.py` would shrink to this:

```python
def route(service, severity):
    svc = SERVICES[service]
    channel = CHANNELS[severity]
    team = svc.get("page_team", svc["team"]) if channel == "page" else svc["team"]
    return team, channel
```

That removes `FINANCE_SERVICES`, `URGENT` and `apply_payments_override`, and "urgent" then simply means "this alert pages someone." It needs Python 3.11 or later for `tomllib`.

Before I build it, you need to settle one thing. The docstring says urgent payments alerts page finance on-call "as well as the owner," but the code replaces billing with `finance-oncall`, so billing never gets paged. If "as well as" is what you want, `page_team` becomes an extra recipient and `route` returns a list of teams. That changes what it returns to callers. Which behaviour is right?

To check that the new version routes the same way as the old one, you could run September's 812 alerts through both and compare the results.
